  "titulo": "Adónde / adonde / dónde / donde",
  "subtitulo": "¿Adónde vas? / ¿Dónde estás? / el lugar adonde vamos.",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "With verbs of movement (ir, llevar, venir), you can use adónde / adonde (or a dónde) or dónde / donde: ¿Adónde vas? = ¿Dónde vas? Without movement, only dónde / donde: ¿Dónde estás? Accent for questions and exclamations; no accent for relatives.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Verb",
            "Possible forms",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "movement (ir, llevar, venir, mudarse)",
              "adónde / a dónde / dónde",
              "¿Adónde vas?"
            ],
            [
              "no movement (estar, vivir, comer)",
              "only dónde / donde",
              "¿Dónde estás?"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Accent rule: **adónde / dónde** in direct and indirect questions and exclamations; **adonde / donde** (no accent) as relatives: **el café adonde vamos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**¿A dónde?** written as two words is also correct and very common in Mexico."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **a** points to a destination, so it only goes with movement."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿==Adónde== vas, Manuel?",
              "en": "Where are you going, Manuel?"
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==A dónde== vas, Manuel?",
              "en": "Where are you going, Manuel?"
            },
            {
              "es": "No sé ==adónde== lleva María esos libros.",
              "en": "I don't know where María is taking those books."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Dónde== están mis lentes?",
              "en": "Where are my glasses?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Cenamos ==donde== tú quieras.",
              "en": "We'll have dinner wherever you want."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿==Adónde== se mudan? —A Mérida.",
              "en": "—Where are you moving to? —To Mérida."
            },
            {
              "es": "No tengo idea de ==dónde== dejé el celular anoche.",
              "en": "I have no idea where I left my phone last night."
            },
            {
              "es": "Vamos a la cafetería ==adonde== fuimos ayer.",
              "en": "Let's go to the café we went to yesterday."
            }
